character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  英 | yīng | flower; petal; outstanding talent; hero | flor; brote; talento sobresaliente; valiente | 艹 | grass / vegetation | 艹 (vegetation / blossoming flowers) | 央 (yāng, central / phonetic) | 8 | 上下结构 | Phono-semantic compound where grass radical 艹 denotes the flowering crest of plants, symbolizing the most radiant, talented blossom among humans. | The central (央) bud bursting into splendid flower (艹) atop the meadow, standing above all others as an elite talent. | El capullo central (央) que florece radiante en el prado (艹), destacando por encima de todos como un talento insigne. | 55 | TLBK | ""
  雄 | xióng | male; grand; powerful; formidable | macho; vigoroso; imponente; poderoso | 隹 | short-tailed bird | 隹 (short-tailed bird / avian strength) | 厷 (gōng, arm muscle / phonetic) | 12 | 左右结构 | Phono-semantic compound where 厷 evokes flexing masculine arm muscles and 隹 represents a majestic soaring raptor, denoting male vitality and commanding grandeur. | A magnificent bird of prey (隹) flexing powerful muscular wings (厷) to dominate the sky with unmatched vigor. | Un ave rapaz majestuosa (隹) que despliega alas musculosas (厷) dominando el firmamento con vigor indomable. | 35 | KCOG | ""

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: Radiant blooming talent (英) fused with indomitable masculine strength (雄) creates an immortal hero (英雄).
  composite_memory_hook_es: El talento floreciente (英) aunado a una fuerza masculina indómita (雄) forja al héroe (英雄) inmortal.
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: Classical Chinese philosophy distinguishes 'yīng' (extraordinary insight and spiritual brilliance) and 'xióng' (physical audacity, military leadership, and sheer willpower). Only those possessing both qualities were hailed as true 英雄, from mythical culture heroes (Yu the Great, Houyi) to folk saviors in festivals.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: High level 1st tone 'yīng' (55) followed by rising 2nd tone 'xióng' (35). The voice glides cleanly upward on 'xióng' without hesitation.

traps_and_cognates:
  look_alikes[5]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,distinction_note}:
    央 | yāng | center; beg | Lacks grass radical 艹 on top
    映 | yìng | reflect; mirror | Has sun radical 日 on the left of 央 instead of 艹 on top
    秧 | yāng | seedling; sprout | Has grain radical 禾 on the left of 央
    难 | nán | difficult; disaster | Has 又 on the left of 隹 instead of 厷
    雅 | yǎ | elegant; refined | Has 牙 on the left of 隹 instead of 厷
  etymological_cognates[5]{character,pinyin,gloss_en}:
