    杰 | jié | outstanding; hero
    勇 | yǒng | brave; courageous
    俊 | jùn | handsome; talented
    魁 | kuí | chief; eminent; giant

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 英雄 emphasizes rare moral courage, extraordinary feats, or selfless sacrifice that earns admiration from a community or civilization.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 英雄 vs. 勇士 | yǒngshì | 英雄 highlights monumental historical deeds, spiritual nobility, and lasting renown, whereas 勇士 focuses primarily on physical battlefield bravery or daring martial skill.
    2 | 英雄 vs. 领袖 | lǐngxiù | 英雄 centers on admired heroism, gallantry, and virtue, whereas 领袖 emphasizes organizational authority, strategic political governance, and leadership over a group or nation.
    3 | 英雄 vs. 偶像 | ǒuxiàng | 英雄 is celebrated for selfless sacrifice, heroic deeds, and collective contributions, while 偶像 denotes an idol or celebrity admired for charm, talent, or popular aesthetic appeal.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 在民间传说中，真正的英雄并非无所不能的神仙，而是在众人畏惧时敢于挺身而出的凡人。正如除夕夜那位持烛而立的老者，以智慧与勇气点燃火光，英雄的意义在于给身处困境的人们带来希望。 | Zài mínjiān chuánshuō zhōng, zhēnzhèng de yīngxióng bìngfēi wúsuǒbùnéng de shénxiān, érshì zài zhòngrén wèijù shí gǎnyú tǐngshēn'érchū de fánrén. Zhèngrú Chúxī yè nà wèi chízhú ér lì de lǎozhě, yǐ zhìhuì yǔ yǒngqì diǎnrán huǒguāng, yīngxióng de yìyì zàiyú gěi shēnchǔ kùnjìng de rénmen dàilái xīwàng. | In folk legends, true heroes are not omnipotent deities, but mortal humans who dare to step forward when others shrink in fear. Just as the elder who stood holding a candle on New Year's Eve igniting flames with wisdom and courage, the essence of a hero lies in bringing hope to people trapped in adversity. | En las leyendas populares, los verdaderos héroes no son deidades omnipotentes, sino personas comunes que dan un paso al frente cuando los demás temen. Al igual que el anciano que encendió la lumbre en fin de año con serenidad y valentía, el sentido del héroe radica en infundir esperanza ante la adversidad.
  #2 | 英雄叙事是连接传统文脉与当代价值的精神纽带。从古代抗击凶险的开拓先驱，到现代危难救援中的奉献者，英雄的内涵虽随时代变迁而演进，但其舍己为人、勇挑重担的精神内核始终历久弥新。 | Yīngxióng xùshì shì liánjiē chuántǒng wénmài yǔ dāngdài jiàzhí de jīngshén niǔdài. Cóng gǔdài kàngjī xiōngxiǎn de kāituò xiānqū, dào xiàndài wēinàn jiùyuán zhōng de fèngxiànzhě, yīngxióng de nèihán suī suí shídài biànqiān ér yǎnjìn, dàn qí shějǐ-wèirén, yǒngtiāo zhòngdān de jīngshén nèihé shǐzhōng jiǔmǐxīn. | Heroic narratives serve as a spiritual bridge linking traditional heritage with contemporary values. From trailblazing pioneers fighting perils in antiquity to selfless rescuers in modern disasters, although the connotations of heroes evolve across eras, their altruism and readiness to bear heavy burdens remain ever vibrant. | La narrativa heroica es el lazo espiritual que une la herencia tradicional con los valores contemporáneos. Desde los pioneros antiguos que combatieron peligros hasta los abnegados rescatistas de hoy, la noción de héroe evoluciona, pero su vocación altruista de cargar con el bienestar ajeno perdura inalterable.